    "updated_at": "2022-05-19T16:27:32Z",
    "body": "So this is a bit different from what I was expecting. What I was expecting is that we create an authority struct on environments upon which we store the various authority-related keys. And then the various algorithms can make use of that in the way that suits them. And over time we migrate keys that are currently stored elsewhere there (or turn them into getters).\r\n\r\nAs in, we need the top-level document site for both networking and storage, should they each be dealing with it individually?",
